{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42829444 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42829444 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42829444","source":"MED","pmid":"42829444","pmcid":"PMC13634210","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13634210"]},"doi":"10.1186/s40104-026-01502-y","title":"Postbiotics enhance immune competence in black rockfish (Sebastes schlegelii): linking innate immunity, apoptosis, and resistance to bacterial infection.","authorString":"Lee SJ, Lee YS, Kim YR, Hwang SB, Jeon MH, Jeong SM, Bae J, Kim MG, Min B, Lee EW, Jang WJ.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Lee SJ","lastName":"Lee","firstName":"Su-Jeong","initials":"SJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Lee YS","lastName":"Lee","firstName":"Young-Sun","initials":"YS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Kim YR","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Yu-Ri","initials":"YR","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Hwang SB","lastName":"Hwang","firstName":"Soo-Bin","initials":"SB","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Jeon MH","lastName":"Jeon","firstName":"Mi-Hyeon","initials":"MH","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Jeong SM","lastName":"Jeong","firstName":"Seong-Mok","initials":"SM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Aquafeed Research Center, National Institute of Fisheries Science, Pohang, 37517, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Bae J","lastName":"Bae","firstName":"Jinho","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Aquafeed Research Center, National Institute of Fisheries Science, Pohang, 37517, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Kim MG","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Min-Gi","initials":"MG","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Aquafeed Research Center, National Institute of Fisheries Science, Pohang, 37517, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Min B","lastName":"Min","firstName":"Byunghwa","initials":"B","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"South Sea Fisheries Research Institute, National Institute of Fisheries Science, Yeosu, 59780, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Lee EW","lastName":"Lee","firstName":"Eun-Woo","initials":"EW","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea. ewlee@deu.ac.kr."},{"affiliation":"Research Institute for Microbiology, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea. ewlee@deu.ac.kr."}]}},{"fullName":"Jang WJ","lastName":"Jang","firstName":"Won Je","initials":"WJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea. wjjang@deu.ac.kr."},{"affiliation":"Research Institute for Microbiology, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea. wjjang@deu.ac.kr."}]}}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"17","journalIssueId":4275140,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Anim Sci Biotechnol","title":"Journal of animal science and biotechnology","essn":"2049-1891","issn":"1674-9782","isoabbreviation":"J Anim Sci Biotechnol","nlmid":"101581293"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"186","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>This study investigated the functional potential and safety of postbiotics derived from Latilactobacillus curvatus NBL2305 as a dietary feed additive for juvenile black rockfish (Sebastes schlegelii). Fish were fed diets supplemented with NBL2305-derived postbiotics, and their effects on growth performance, immune responses, antioxidant capacity, apoptosis-related gene expression, intestinal microbiota, and disease resistance were evaluated.<h4>Results</h4>Supplementation with postbiotics significantly improved growth performance and feed utilization, as indicated by increased weight gain and specific growth rate, along with a reduced feed conversion ratio. Innate immune responses were enhanced, as demonstrated by elevated activities of myeloperoxidase, superoxide dismutase, and lysozyme together with the upregulated expression of immune-related genes, including il8, il1b, tnfa, tnfsf13b, and nfkb1. In addition, postbiotic treatment modulated apoptosis-related gene expression in the liver, characterized by the downregulation of pro-apoptotic genes (bax, tp53, and casp3) and the upregulation of anti-apoptotic genes (bcl2 and xiap), indicating an anti-apoptotic gene expression profile. The postbiotics also exhibited strong antimicrobial activity against major fish pathogens and considerable antioxidant capacity. These functional effects were further supported by an in vivo challenge test, in which the postbiotic-fed group showed significantly higher survival following Edwardsiella tarda infection. No adverse effects were observed in serum biochemical parameters, somatic indices, or histopathological analyses, supporting the short-term safety of supplementation under the experimental conditions evaluated. Moreover, the intestinal microbiota composition remained stable, with selective enrichment of beneficial taxa.<h4>Conclusions</h4>Collectively, these findings demonstrate that NBL2305-derived postbiotics are safe and effective functional feed additives that enhance growth, modulated innate immune responses, and disease resistance in aquaculture species.","affiliation":"Department of Biomedicine and Pharmaceutics, Dong-Eui University, Busan, 47340, Korea.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Korea Basic Science Institute","grantId":"RS-2024-00403688","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institute of Fisheries Science","grantId":"R2026038","orderIn":0}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Disease resistance","Apoptosis","Microbiota","Immune modulation","Postbiotics"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40104-026-01502-y"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13634210"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13634210?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["refseq"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-10-03","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-03","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-06","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-04","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-04","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-04","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-10-06","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}